{"duration_api_ms":11158,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"3860df9a-166f-420b-93f6-9ed48b1453bf","total_cost_usd":0.0013173,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":695,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":1501,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1108},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":695,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1501,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":695,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":695},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-5-5":{"inputTokens":1238,"outputTokens":2109,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":695,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.0013173,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":1689,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":695,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"I can't see the reviewed AP forms, so this is a general framework, not a clause-level review. Please paste the relevant sections if you need specifics.\n\n**US (Rule 6c-11):** The rule sets conditions for ETFs to operate without individual exemptive relief, including custom-basket policies and daily disclosure. It doesn't prescribe AP agreement parties. In practice, the AP agreement is typically signed by the issuing trust (usually a Delaware statutory trust) on behalf of a specific fund series, with the principal underwriter/distributor and the authorized participant (a broker-dealer and DTC participant) as counterparties. The trust has no separate legal personality, so the signature block and series designation matter.\n\n**Ireland (ICAV):** An ICAV is a corporate vehicle with separate legal personality under the ICAV Act 2015, governed by a board and Central Bank of Ireland UCITS rules. Its umbrella structure gives statutory segregation between sub-funds. Participating dealers sign agreements with the ICAV and its distributor, and a UCITS depositary plays an oversight role with no direct US equivalent. Rule 6c-11 has no Irish analogue.","ttft_ms":6292,"type":"result","duration_ms":8122,"uuid":"b22732a9-527d-4449-9edc-0ce9e64b246e","ttft_stream_ms":437,"time_to_request_ms":50,"first_content_frame_ms":437,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-28T06:36:39.484Z"}
